# paradigmxyz/reth#26843 "fix(trie): correctly handle branch collapse in proof
# v2". With a prefix set (a historical overlay's reverted keys), proof v2 drops
# a clean sibling under a stored branch stack and returns a wrong storage root.
# #27634 (078d026) later stopped historical overlays from passing prefix sets,
# so the patch also reverts it. #26843 itself no longer reverts cleanly: the
# patch restores proof_v2/{mod,node}.rs from its parent, which also drops
# #26973, #27019, #27408 and #27567 from proof v2; triage hits against those.
RETH_PATCH=reth-26843.patch
# reth#27615 (unmerged) produces the same E5/E6 multiproof-* and untargeted-*
# signatures on the pinned node; apply it to both images.
BASE_RETH_PRS="27615:30904dc4158defd496565da8f28671af81096091"
VARIANT=default
CAMPAIGN_ARGS="--workload-arg load=trie"
EXPECT=E5/multiproof-storage-root-mismatch
